committer alexeikarp <ak@hrbr.life> 1790255068 +0400

test(estate): the runner funds the owner-signed margin, not just the listing floor (review of 8387442)

8387442 lets the owners sign an operator balance above the seed-listing
floor (a margin for later promotes) and fund-root-store-operator tops up to
that signed target. No test ran the runner with a target above the floor, so
a runner that probed or topped up only to the derived floor (requiredLamports)
passed every test: the owners' signed margin would be silently dropped.

The new test pre-funds the operator with exactly the floor, signs floor +
7,000,000, and requires the probe to report not-done, one transfer to the
signed balance, a readback naming both figures, and convergence.

Mutation controls, each restored: probe `balance < required` and run
`balance >= required` / `required - balance` each fail this test by name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
